## 8.2 Case Study Valuation: Apple Inc.'s Owner Earnings
To understand Warren Buffett's real-world strategy, we can calculate Apple Inc.’s Owner Earnings using its Form 10-K filed with the SEC. 

### Calculation Protocol
1.  **Extract Raw Elements (FY 2025):** Collect Net Income, D&A, SBC, and Total CapEx from audited statements.
2.  **Separate Growth CapEx from Maintenance CapEx:** Review Note 1 (Summary of Significant Accounting Policies) and the MD&A section. Use a 3-year rolling average of its D&A profile as a proxy for Maintenance CapEx.
3.  **Execute the Calculation:**
    $$\text{Owner Earnings} = \text{Net Income} + \text{D\&A} + \text{SBC} - \text{Maintenance CapEx} \pm \Delta \text{Working Capital}$$

This analysis demonstrates why Buffett maintains a massive equity stake in Apple: the business converts a high percentage of its net income into unencumbered Owner Earnings, confirming its capital efficiency.

